 },
 "duration": 344.688,
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "h01",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "One Tuesday, the same envelope lands in five mailboxes.",
   "refs": [
    "=5"
   ],
   "start": 0.4,
   "end": 4.079,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "h02",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "Inside is a surprise dental bill for one thousand two hundred dollars.",
   "refs": [
    "bill"
   ],
   "start": 4.499,
   "end": 8.642,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "h03",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "Same bill, same month, but five very different paychecks.",
   "refs": [
    "=5"
   ],
   "start": 9.062,
   "end": 12.426,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "h04",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "Sam takes home two thousand four hundred dollars a month.",
   "refs": [
    "sam.income"
   ],
   "start": 12.846,
   "end": 15.789,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "h05",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "Richard takes home twenty-two thousand.",
   "refs": [
    "richard.income"
   ],
   "start": 16.209,
   "end": 18.566,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "h06",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "So Richard handles it best, right?",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 18.986,
   "end": 20.982,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "h07",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "Not so fast. Income isn't what decides who stays calm this month.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 21.402,
   "end": 25.732,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "h08",
   "section": "hook",
   "text": "Something else does, and by the end, you'll spot it in your own budget.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 26.152,
   "end": 29.819,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "r01",
   "section": "rules",
   "text": "Here's the experiment.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 30.619,
   "end": 31.99,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "r02",
   "section": "rules",
   "text": "Five people, the same month, and the same one thousand two hundred dollar bill.",
   "refs": [
    "=5",
    "bill"
   ],
   "start": 32.41,
   "end": 36.746,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "r03",
   "section": "rules",
   "text": "They're made-up people with simplified budgets, and every number is an example.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 37.166,
   "end": 41.717,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "r04",
   "section": "rules",
   "text": "For each of them, we'll look at what comes in, what goes out, and what's left.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 42.137,
   "end": 45.923,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "r05",
   "section": "rules",
   "text": "Keep score as we go: who stays calm, and who doesn't?",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 46.343,
   "end": 49.445,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "l01",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Level one: meet Sam.",
   "refs": [
    "=1"
   ],
   "start": 50.245,
   "end": 51.809,
   "chunk": 0
  },
  {
   "id": "l02",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Sam is twenty-four, works in retail, and brings home two thousand four hundred dollars a month.",
   "refs": [
    "=24",
    "sam.income"
   ],
   "start": 52.229,
   "end": 57.754,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l03",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Rent on a shared apartment, utilities, groceries, the bus and health insurance take two thousand one hundred seventy.",
   "refs": [
    "sam.fixed_total"
   ],
   "start": 58.174,
   "end": 65.086,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l04",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Then come the little leaks: eighty dollars of delivery fees and a late fee.",
   "refs": [
    "sam.leaks_total"
   ],
   "start": 65.506,
   "end": 69.797,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l05",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "That leaves Sam one hundred fifty dollars a month, with just two hundred in savings.",
   "refs": [
    "sam.left_over",
    "sam.savings"
   ],
   "start": 70.217,
   "end": 75.098,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l06",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Then, on Tuesday, the envelope arrives.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 75.518,
   "end": 77.915,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l07",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "One thousand two hundred dollars, due in thirty days.",
   "refs": [
    "bill",
    "bill_due_days"
   ],
   "start": 78.335,
   "end": 81.591,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l08",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Sam can't cover it, so Sam does something simple, and asks.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 82.011,
   "end": 85.349,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l09",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "The dentist's office agrees to a payment plan.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 85.769,
   "end": 88.401,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l10",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Two hundred from savings now, then one hundred dollars a month for ten months.",
   "refs": [
    "sam.savings",
    "sam.plan_monthly",
    "sam.plan_months"
   ],
   "start": 88.821,
   "end": 93.253,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l11",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "It fits inside Sam's one hundred fifty dollar gap, just.",
   "refs": [
    "sam.left_over"
   ],
   "start": 93.673,
   "end": 97.12,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l12",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "It's tight, but Sam isn't panicking, because Sam has a plan.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 97.54,
   "end": 100.777,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "l13",
   "section": "level1",
   "text": "Sam's habit: turning on autopay, so those late fees stop for good.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 101.197,
   "end": 105.19,
   "chunk": 1
  },
  {
   "id": "n01",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "Level two: meet Nina.",
   "refs": [
    "=2"
   ],
   "start": 105.99,
   "end": 107.57,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n02",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "Nina works in an office and takes home three thousand eight hundred a month.",
   "refs": [
    "nina.income"
   ],
   "start": 107.99,
   "end": 111.678,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n03",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "Rent, her car, groceries, bills and a student loan take two thousand nine hundred ninety.",
   "refs": [
    "nina.fixed_total"
   ],
   "start": 112.098,
   "end": 117.116,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n04",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "Takeout and subscriptions take another one hundred eighty-four.",
   "refs": [
    "nina.leaks_total"
   ],
   "start": 117.536,
   "end": 121.121,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n05",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "That leaves her six hundred twenty-six a month, and over time she's saved two thousand.",
   "refs": [
    "nina.left_over",
    "nina.savings"
   ],
   "start": 121.541,
   "end": 126.621,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n06",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "The bill arrives, and her savings cover all of it, with eight hundred to spare.",
   "refs": [
    "nina.savings_after_bill"
   ],
   "start": 127.041,
   "end": 131.366,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n07",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "But even Nina has a surprise.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 131.786,
   "end": 133.794,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n08",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "Checking her statement, she finds sixty-four dollars a month of subscriptions she forgot she had.",
   "refs": [
    "nina.leak:forgotten_subscriptions"
   ],
   "start": 134.214,
   "end": 139.696,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n09",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "She cancels them that night, and that money goes straight back into her buffer.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 140.116,
   "end": 144.283,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n10",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "Nina's habit: a ten-minute leak check at the start of every month.",
   "refs": [
    "=10"
   ],
   "start": 144.703,
   "end": 148.439,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "n11",
   "section": "level2",
   "text": "Remember Nina. And stick around, because the biggest paycheck in this video hides the biggest surprise.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 148.859,
   "end": 154.828,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "c01",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "Level three: meet Claire.",
   "refs": [
    "=3"
   ],
   "start": 155.628,
   "end": 157.254,
   "chunk": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "c02",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "Claire got a promotion last year, and now takes home five thousand six hundred a month.",
   "refs": [
    "claire.income"
   ],
   "start": 157.674,
   "end": 162.532,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c03",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "Her fixed costs are three thousand nine hundred thirty, including the minimum on a credit card.",
   "refs": [
    "claire.fixed_total"
   ],
   "start": 162.952,
   "end": 168.195,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c04",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "But look at the leaks: one thousand five hundred a month on dining out, shopping and subscriptions.",
   "refs": [
    "claire.leaks_total"
   ],
   "start": 168.615,
   "end": 173.993,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c05",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "When her pay went up, her spending quietly went up with it.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 174.413,
   "end": 177.461,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c06",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "So she has just one hundred seventy left each month, and six hundred saved.",
   "refs": [
    "claire.left_over",
    "claire.savings"
   ],
   "start": 177.881,
   "end": 182.242,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c07",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "The bill arrives, and the six hundred her savings can't cover goes on the credit card.",
   "refs": [
    "claire.bill_shortfall"
   ],
   "start": 182.662,
   "end": 187.422,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c08",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "Now that bill grows with interest, on top of the balance she already had.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 187.842,
   "end": 192.07,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c09",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "Claire earns more than double what Sam does, but her monthly gap is only twenty dollars bigger.",
   "refs": [
    "=20"
   ],
   "start": 192.49,
   "end": 198.223,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "c10",
   "section": "level3",
   "text": "Claire's habit: the next time her pay goes up, half the raise goes straight to savings.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 198.643,
   "end": 203.486,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "m01",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "Level four: meet Marcus.",
   "refs": [
    "=4"
   ],
   "start": 204.286,
   "end": 206.132,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "m02",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "Marcus works in tech and takes home nine thousand five hundred a month.",
   "refs": [
    "marcus.income"
   ],
   "start": 206.552,
   "end": 210.651,
   "chunk": 3
  },
  {
   "id": "m03",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "But big-city rent, a car lease, childcare and student loans add up to seven thousand eight hundred eighty.",
   "refs": [
    "marcus.fixed_total"
   ],
   "start": 211.071,
   "end": 217.467,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "m04",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "That's eighty-three cents of every dollar, gone before the month even starts.",
   "refs": [
    "marcus.fixed_share_pct"
   ],
   "start": 217.887,
   "end": 222.189,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "m05",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "With five hundred twenty in leaks, he has one thousand one hundred left, and one thousand five hundred saved.",
   "refs": [
    "marcus.leaks_total",
    "marcus.left_over",
    "marcus.savings"
   ],
   "start": 222.609,
   "end": 228.703,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "m06",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "The bill arrives, and his savings cover it.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 229.123,
   "end": 231.332,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "m07",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "But that leaves just three hundred in the bank, with costs this high.",
   "refs": [
    "marcus.savings_after_bill"
   ],
   "start": 231.752,
   "end": 235.345,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "m08",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "One more surprise, and Marcus is in trouble.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 235.765,
   "end": 238.452,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "m09",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "A car repair or a childcare bill next month would hit an almost empty account.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 238.872,
   "end": 243.498,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "m10",
   "section": "level4",
   "text": "Marcus's habit: rebuilding that buffer first, before taking on anything new.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 243.918,
   "end": 248.409,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "x01",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "Level five: meet Richard.",
   "refs": [
    "=5"
   ],
   "start": 249.209,
   "end": 250.953,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "x02",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "Richard takes home twenty-two thousand a month, more than nine times what Sam earns.",
   "refs": [
    "richard.income",
    "richard.income_multiple_vs_level1"
   ],
   "start": 251.373,
   "end": 256.393,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "x03",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "His mortgage, two car payments, private school and a housekeeper add up to eighteen thousand one hundred fifty.",
   "refs": [
    "=2",
    "richard.fixed_total"
   ],
   "start": 256.813,
   "end": 263.056,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "x04",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "And here's the biggest surprise in this video.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 263.476,
   "end": 265.904,
   "chunk": 4
  },
  {
   "id": "x05",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "Richard's leaks are two thousand nine hundred fifty a month.",
   "refs": [
    "richard.leaks_total"
   ],
   "start": 266.324,
   "end": 269.545,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "x06",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "His leaks alone are bigger than Sam's entire paycheck.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 269.965,
   "end": 273.212,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "x07",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "That leaves nine hundred a month, and one thousand saved.",
   "refs": [
    "richard.left_over",
    "richard.savings"
   ],
   "start": 273.632,
   "end": 276.817,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "x08",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "The bill arrives, and Richard is the one who panics.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 277.237,
   "end": 280.077,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "x09",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "Paying it takes all his savings, plus two hundred more, and leaves him with no buffer at all.",
   "refs": [
    "richard.bill_shortfall"
   ],
   "start": 280.497,
   "end": 285.566,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "x10",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "Earning nine times more than Sam didn't buy him a calmer month.",
   "refs": [
    "=9"
   ],
   "start": 285.986,
   "end": 289.559,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "x11",
   "section": "level5",
   "text": "Richard's habit, starting now: a monthly leak check, just like Nina's.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 289.979,
   "end": 294.268,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "t01",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "So who stayed calmest?",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 295.068,
   "end": 296.564,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "t02",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "Not Richard, with the biggest paycheck. It was Nina.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 296.984,
   "end": 300.194,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "t03",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "Income didn't decide who coped. The gap between earning and spending did, and a small buffer.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 300.614,
   "end": 306.124,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "t04",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "Sam had a plan. Nina had a buffer. Claire had a credit card. Marcus had a thin cushion. And Richard had nothing left.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 306.544,
   "end": 313.615,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "t05",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "Here are three takeaways.",
   "refs": [
    "=3"
   ],
   "start": 314.035,
   "end": 315.695,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "t06",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "One: know your monthly gap, what's left after everything goes out.",
   "refs": [
    "=1"
   ],
   "start": 316.115,
   "end": 319.907,
   "chunk": 5
  },
  {
   "id": "t07",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "Two: build a starter buffer, even a small one.",
   "refs": [
    "=2"
   ],
   "start": 320.327,
   "end": 322.934,
   "chunk": 6
  },
  {
   "id": "t08",
   "section": "twist",
   "text": "Three: hunt your leaks every month, because they quietly widen or close that gap.",
   "refs": [
    "=3"
   ],
   "start": 323.354,
   "end": 327.861,
   "chunk": 6
  },
  {
   "id": "e01",
   "section": "cta",
   "text": "Check out the Money Leak Audit Workbook in the description. It walks you through finding your own leaks.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 328.661,
   "end": 334.319,
   "chunk": 6
  },
  {
   "id": "e02",
   "section": "cta",
   "text": "Fill it in once, and you'll see your own gap in black and white.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 334.739,
   "end": 338.129,
   "chunk": 6
  },
  {
   "id": "e03",
   "section": "cta",
   "text": "And remember, this video is educational only, not financial advice.",
   "refs": [],
   "start": 338.549,
   "end": 343.088,
   "chunk": 6
  }
 ],
